#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Regenerate the Datasworn-sourced adapters' content. Standard library only.

Datasworn (https://github.com/rsek/datasworn) publishes Shawn Tomkin's Ironsworn-family
games as machine-readable JSON. This tool converts pinned copies of two of its files into
the gm adapters' formats:

  starforged.json      -> adapters/starforged/      the Starforged SRD (a ruleset)
  sundered_isles.json  -> adapters/sundered-isles/  Sundered Isles (an expansion of it)

For each adapter it writes:

  oracles/**/*.md           every rollable table (`roll table` format)
  rules/oracles.md          an index of the tables in force
  rules/moves.md            the full move list
  rules/assets.md           the asset index, and the asset cards by category
  rules/truths.md           the setting truths
  sheet-template.md         the character sheet
  tests/fixtures/oracles/<adapter>/**/*.json   golden ranges for tests/test_oracle_parity.py

An expansion's adapter `extends:` its ruleset's, and the gm core unions their files by
path, the child's winning. So the expansion's adapter carries only what the expansion
changes:
  - a table the expansion `replaces` is written at the replaced table's path, so it wins
    there and every reference to the old table reaches the new one;
  - a ruleset table it replaces with nothing at that path (one inside a replaced
    collection, say) gets a one-entry redirect table there, naming the replacement;
  - its rules/moves.md is the ruleset's move list with the expansion's versions in place,
    and rules/oracles.md, rules/assets.md and rules/truths.md cover the whole set in force;
  - its own asset cards go to rules/assets/<adapter>/<category>.md, beside the ruleset's
    cards, which still apply.
Any other path an expansion table shares with a ruleset table is an error, unless SHADOWS
lists it.

The tool owns its output: a run deletes every file it generated before (each .md starts
with the GENERATED marker; the fixture dirs are all its own) and writes the new set, so
edit this tool or its pins, never the output. Hand-written adapter files (adapter.md,
SOURCE.md, frames/, rules/campaign-launch.md, rules/character-creation.md,
rules/sector-creation.md) have no marker and are never touched; a generated path that
would overwrite one is an error.

Usage:
  datasworn-import                  fetch the pinned upstream files, verify, regenerate
  datasworn-import --json FILE ...  use local copies of pinned files instead; each is
                                    matched to its pin by sha256, the rest are fetched
  datasworn-import --check          regenerate in memory and diff against the tree
                                    (exit 1 on any drift; CI runs this)

To move the pins: change UPSTREAM_REF and UPSTREAM_TAG and each package's sha256 in
PACKAGES, re-run, review the diff, and update the adapters' SOURCE.md and NOTICE.
"""
